---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { relFor } from '../../lib/affiliate-value';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import CategoryHub from '../../components/CategoryHub.astro';
import AffiliateDisclosure from '../../components/AffiliateDisclosure.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Donation processing software for nonprofits"
  description="Donorbox vs Zeffy vs 4aGoodCause and more: what online donation platforms cost after platform and processing fees, and the volume where a flat fee beats a percentage."
  section="donation-processing">
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Donation processing' }]} />
    <section class="prose" style="margin-top: 1.2rem;">
      <p class="kicker">Category guide</p>
      <h1>Donation processing software</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Donation platforms take the money: forms, recurring gifts, and the fees
        on every gift. Genuinely free options compete head-on with paid ones
        here, so the real comparison is the fee math on your volume. And not
        every organization needs a CRM first — a processor keeps donor records
        of its own, so for many small shops it is the honest first step, with
        the <a href="/donor-crm/">database decision</a> coming later.
      </p>

      <AffiliateDisclosure />
    </section>

    <CategoryHub category="donation-processing" part="table" />


    <section class="prose" style="max-width: none;">


      <h2>How to choose</h2>
      <p>
        Three fee models compete, and your annual online volume decides between
        them before any feature does.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>A percentage of every gift.</strong>
        <a href="/go/donorbox" rel={relFor('donorbox')}>Donorbox</a> takes about
        2.95% (roughly 1.75% on Pro) and gives you the deepest recurring-gift
        tooling in the class: failed-card recovery, donor portals and CRM
        integrations. Nothing to pay until money moves, which makes it the right
        first platform for almost every small shop.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>A flat subscription.</strong>
        <a href="/go/4agoodcause" rel={relFor('4agoodcause')}>4aGoodCause</a>
        charges from $99 a month and takes no cut of donations. The crossover
        against Donorbox's standard rate is about <strong>$40,270</strong> of
        online giving a year: below it the percentage is cheaper, above it the
        flat fee wins and the gap widens every year your program grows. The
        year-by-year math is on <a href="/platforms/4agoodcause/">our 4aGoodCause
        page</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Free, funded by donor tips.</strong>
        <a href="/go/zeffy" rel={relFor('zeffy')}>Zeffy</a> charges the nonprofit
        nothing at any volume, and
        <a href="/go/givebutter" rel={relFor('givebutter')}>Givebutter</a> is 0%
        with tips on. The tradeoff is that your effective rate depends on how
        many donors leave the tip in place, which you do not control.
      </p>
      <p>
        Do the arithmetic on last year's online total first, then test the
        donor-facing checkout on your phone. Donor experience moves conversion
        more than a fee point does, and every platform here will let you try a
        live form before you commit.
      </p>
    </section>


    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        See how the processing line is sized in <a href="/stacks/under-250k/">the
        grassroots stack</a>, <a href="/stacks/250k-1m/">the $250k-$1M stack</a>
        and <a href="/stacks/1m-5m/">$1M-$5M</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
